; =====================================================================
; figure-6-1-uri-v2.2-compatible.derived.abnf
;
; DERIVED - not verbatim. Figure 6-1 of NISTIR 7695 (CPE Naming
; Specification Version 2.3, August 2011), "ABNF for v2.2-Compatible
; URI Binding", section 6.1.1, printed page 16, repaired so that it is
; valid RFC 5234 ABNF. The verbatim figure is
; figure-6-1-uri-v2.2-compatible.abnf beside this file.
;
; Root rule: cpe-name.
;
; Source PDF SHA-256
; 01553a4638b21eda10018690b71162e91605d78eb15850f881bd0b2b691ac3f6
;
; Role. 6.1.1 says: "To ensure full backward compatibility with
; [CPE22], any implementation that consumes URIs and claims to be
; conformant with this Naming specification MUST accept as valid input
; any URI that obeys the full syntax shown in Figure 6-1." Section 4,
; item 3: "If the implementation produces CPE names in URI form, it
; MUST produce URIs that adhere to the syntax rules specified in
; Figure 6-1".
;
; The three repairs, and nothing else (every other token is the
; figure's):
;   R1  "/=" is written "=/". RFC 2234 section 3.3 (and RFC 5234
;       section 3.3) spells incremental alternatives "=/"; "/=" is not
;       ABNF.
;   R2  The last alternative of unreserved is printed as U+02DC SMALL
;       TILDE (the PDF's text layer and its glyph agree). It is written
;       "~" (ASCII tilde, %x7E) here: a char-val may hold only %x20-21
;       and %x23-7E, the CPE 2.2 grammar that 6.1.1 says this figure
;       shows lists "~" among its punctuation, and 6.1.3.3.7 says "The
;       original v2.2 URI syntax allows tildes to appear without
;       encoding".
;   R3  "LANGTAG = cf. [RFC5646]" is prose, not ABNF. It is written as
;       an ABNF prose value. run-fixtures.derived.py supplies it: the
;       RFC 5646 section 2.1 Language-Tag production (well-formedness
;       only).
;
; Reading kept from the figure, not repaired: RFC 2234 quoted strings
; are case-insensitive, so "cpe:/", "h", "o", "a" and the hex digits
; "a" to "f" match in either case. run-fixtures.derived.py also reports
; a case-sensitive reading (every quoted string as RFC 7405 %s"...")
; because the XML schema the specification calls authoritative is
; case-sensitive; README.md compares the two.
; =====================================================================

cpe-name                = "cpe:/" component-list

component-list          = part ":" vendor ":" product ":" version ":" update ":"
                          edition ":" lang
component-list          =/ part ":" vendor ":" product ":" version ":" update ":"
                           edition
component-list          =/ part ":" vendor ":" product ":" version ":" update
component-list          =/ part ":" vendor ":" product ":" version
component-list          =/ part ":" vendor ":" product
component-list          =/ part ":" vendor
component-list          =/ part
component-list          =/ empty
part                    = "h" / "o" / "a" / empty
vendor                  = string
product                 = string
version                 = string
update                  = string
edition                 = string
lang                    = LANGTAG / empty
string                  = *( unreserved / pct-encoded )
empty                   = ""
unreserved              = ALPHA / DIGIT / "-" / "." / "_" / "~"
pct-encoded             = "%" HEXDIG HEXDIG
ALPHA                   = %x41-5a / %x61-7a   ; A-Z or a-z
DIGIT                   = %x30-39 ; 0-9
HEXDIG                  = DIGIT / "a" / "b" / "c" / "d" / "e" / "f"
LANGTAG                 = <Language-Tag, RFC 5646 section 2.1>
